„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections—…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Ye are the children of the LORD your God: ye shall not cut yourselves, nor make any baldness between your eyes for the dead.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥For thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God, and the LORD hath chosen thee to be a peculiar people unto himself, above all the nations that are upon the earth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ(Thou shalt not eat any abominable thing.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIThese are the beasts which ye shall eat: the ox, the sheep, and the goat,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtthe hart, and the roebuck, and the fallow deer, and the wild goat, and the pygarg, and the wild ox, and the chamois.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And every beast that parteth the hoof, and cleaveth the cleft into two claws, and cheweth the cud among the beasts, that ye shall eat.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙæNevertheless these ye shall not eat of them that chew the cud, or of them that divide the cloven hoof; as the camel, and the hare, and the coney: for they chew the cud, but divide not the hoof; therefore they are unclean unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd the swine, because it divideth the hoof, yet cheweth not the cud, it is unclean unto you: ye shall not eat of their flesh, nor touch their dead carcase.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse
