 of thine oil, and the firstlings of thy herds and of thy flocks; that thou mayest learn to fear the LORD thy God always.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÕAnd if the way be too long for thee, so that thou art not able to carry it; or if the place be too far from thee, which the LORD thy God shall choose to set his name there, when the LORD thy God hath blessed thee:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰then shalt thou turn it into money, and bind up the money in thine hand, and shalt go unto the place which the LORD thy God shall choose:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚand thou shalt bestow that money for whatsoever thy soul lusteth after, for oxen, or for sheep, or for wine, or for strong drink, or for whatsoever thy soul desireth: and thou shalt eat there before the LORD thy God, and thou shalt rejoice, thou, and thine household,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsand the Levite that is within thy gates; thou shalt not forsake him; for he hath no part nor inheritance with thee.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…At the end of three years thou shalt bring forth all the tithe of thine increase the same year, and shalt lay it up within thy gates:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚand the Levite, (because he hath no part nor inheritance with thee,) and the stranger, and the fatherless, and the widow, which are within thy gates, shall come, and shall eat and be satisfied; that the LORD thy God may bless thee in all the work of thine hand which thou doest.¦layout ªlast_verse